@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home Page";
}

<div class="jumbotron">
    <h1>StoreFactory Web Simulator</h1>
    <p class="lead">Digital lab for understanding fabric shrinkage during automated textile production.</p>
    <p class="text-muted">This site lets you simulate heat-setting parameters, inspect data-driven insights, and review performance benchmarks for parallel computation.</p>
    <p>
        <a asp-controller="Simulator" asp-action="Index" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Open Simulator &raquo;</a>
        <a asp-controller="Analysis" asp-action="Index" class="btn btn-default btn-lg">View Analysis &raquo;</a>
    </p>
</div>

<div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-12">
        <div class="panel panel-default sf-analysis-summary">
            <div class="panel-heading">What you can do here</div>
            <div class="panel-body">
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <div class="sf-metric">
                            <div class="sf-metric-label">Simulator</div>
                            <div class="sf-metric-value">Model shrinkage</div>
                            <div class="sf-metric-sub">Tune temperature and dwell time to see predicted fabric changes.</div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <div class="sf-metric">
                            <div class="sf-metric-label">Analysis</div>
                            <div class="sf-metric-value">Explain trends</div>
                            <div class="sf-metric-sub">Review curves, surfaces, and risk indicators from measured data.</div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <div class="sf-metric">
                            <div class="sf-metric-label">Performance</div>
                            <div class="sf-metric-value">Benchmark speed</div>
                            <div class="sf-metric-sub">See parallel processing speedups on synthetic workloads.</div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-12">
        <div class="page-header sf-page-header">
            <h2>Thesis Context <small>StoreFactory production chain overview</small></h2>
            <p class="text-muted">This web simulator highlights the shrinkage-aware Converter Unit and its impact on downstream production.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-7">
        <div class="well">
            <h4>Abstract</h4>
            <p>
                This work focuses on the technical implementation of the StoreFactory project that is
                a part of the federal Industry 4.0 programme. It looks into the entire cycle of tailored
                garments production from body scanning to knitting the final product, and proposes a
                way to automate the whole process to the highest degree.
            </p>
            <p>
                Objective of this Thesis: Automating the textile production chain by joining body
                scanners and knitting machines into a homogenous solution that implies minimal
                human intervention and further decreases manufacturing costs of garments.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-5">
        <h3>Project Components</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Global Controller (GC) - Central management utility</li>
            <li>Converter Unit (CU) - Adjusts measurements for shrinkage</li>
            <li>Database (DB) - Stores material parameters</li>
            <li>XMLTool - Generates PPS job files</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>How to use this web simulator</h3>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Simulator:</strong> choose a material, temperature, and dwell time to see shrinkage factors.</li>
            <li><strong>Insights:</strong> review curves and surface plots to understand trends.</li>
            <li><strong>Analysis:</strong> open the analysis dashboards for aggregated data and risk summaries.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>
